{
  "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
  "student_id": "stu-demo-c",
  "session_index": 4,
  "session_date": "2026-02-03",
  "session_topic": "Scaling a ratio",
  "has_timestamps": true,
  "transcript_scope": "full",
  "problems": [
    {
      "problem_id": "demo-c-s04-p01",
      "topic": "Scaling a ratio",
      "start_turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t001",
      "end_turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t058"
    }
  ],
  "turns": [
    {
      "_id": "0",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "A recipe uses flour and sugar in a 3 to 5 ratio, and we're told 12 cups of flour are used. Let's figure out how much sugar that needs.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t001",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:00:00.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:00:44.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "1",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 2,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So the ratio is 3 parts flour to 5 parts sugar, and we know the flour is 12 cups.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t002",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:00:51.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:01:33.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "2",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 3,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, and the question just wants the matching amount of sugar.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t003",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:01:33.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:02:11.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "3",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 4,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Got it — we need to find the sugar amount that keeps that same ratio.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t004",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:02:17.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:02:52.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "4",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 5,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Since 3 parts equal 12 cups, let's divide 12 by 3 to see what one part is worth.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t005",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:02:53.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:03:43.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "5",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 6,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "12 divided by 3 is 4, so one part is 4 cups.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t006",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:03:43.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:04:05.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "6",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 7,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good, now sugar is 5 parts, so multiply 4 by 5.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t007",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:04:10.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:04:49.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "7",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 8,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "4 times 5 is 20.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t008",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:04:51.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:05:12.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "8",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 9,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "So the sugar amount comes out to 20 cups.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t009",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:05:12.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:06:15.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "9",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 10,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "20 cups of sugar for 12 cups of flour.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t010",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:06:19.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:06:58.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "10",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 11,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That gives us our answer, so the core calculation is done.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t011",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:06:58.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:07:20.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "11",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 12,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "I wonder if there's a different way to get there, like setting up a proportion instead.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t012",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:07:25.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:07:40.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "12",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 13,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Sure, what would that proportion look like?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t013",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:07:41.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:08:48.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "13",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 14,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Maybe 3 over 5 equals 12 over some unknown sugar amount?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t014",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:08:49.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:09:25.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "14",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 15,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's worth trying out properly.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t015",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:09:33.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:10:14.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "15",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 16,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Okay, so I should set up the proportion and then solve for the unknown.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t016",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:10:22.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:11:29.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "16",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 17,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Yes, what's the first move to solve it?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t017",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:11:29.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:12:13.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "17",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 18,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "I'll cross-multiply the two sides of the proportion.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t018",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:12:20.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:12:37.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "18",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 19,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "And what will that give you before you simplify?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t019",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:12:39.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:13:13.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "19",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 20,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "It'll give an equation with the unknown times 3 equal to 5 times 12.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t020",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:13:19.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:14.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "20",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 21,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Then what do you do with that equation?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t021",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:15.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:47.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "21",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 22,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Divide both sides by 3 to isolate the unknown.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t022",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:49.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:15:46.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "22",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 23,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Sounds like a solid plan, go ahead and work it.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t023",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:15:46.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:16:26.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "23",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 24,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Let me write 3 over 5 equals 12 over x and cross-multiply.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t024",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:16:31.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:16:47.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "24",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 25,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go ahead, what do you get?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t025",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:16:54.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:17:27.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "25",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 26,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "3 times x equals 5 times 12, so 3x equals 60.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t026",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:17:32.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:18:11.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "26",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 27,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Now divide both sides by 3 to finish.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t027",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:18:11.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:19:16.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "27",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 28,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Let me just write x equals 20 cups clearly on my sheet.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t028",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:19:16.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:19:41.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "28",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 29,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Perfect, jot that down so we've got both methods recorded.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t029",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:19:41.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:20:14.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "29",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 30,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So both the parts method and the proportion method landed on 20 — that makes sense since they're really the same idea.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t030",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:20:17.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:20:32.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "30",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 31,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, why do you think they always agree?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t031",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:20:34.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:21:21.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "31",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 32,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Because a ratio just means flour and sugar scale up by the same factor.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t032",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:21:25.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:22:01.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "32",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 33,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Exactly, so 12 cups of flour is 4 times the 3 in the ratio.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t033",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:22:09.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:22:50.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "33",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 34,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So sugar has to scale by that same factor of 4 from the 5.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t034",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:22:54.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:23:57.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "34",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 35,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's the key idea tying both methods together.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t035",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:24:02.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:24:18.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "35",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 36,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "What if we doubled the whole recipe — would the ratio still work out the same way?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t036",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:24:24.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:24:52.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "36",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 37,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Try it and see what happens to the numbers.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t037",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:24:54.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:25:29.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "37",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 38,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Doubling would make it 24 cups of flour and maybe 40 cups of sugar?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t038",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:25:34.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:26:38.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "38",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 39,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Check whether 24 to 40 still simplifies the same way.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t039",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:26:41.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:27:30.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "39",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 40,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "24 over 40 simplifies to 3 over 5 if I divide both by 8.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t040",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:27:33.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:28:32.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "40",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 41,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "So the ratio held even after doubling — what does that tell you?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t041",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:28:33.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:28:58.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "41",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 42,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "It tells me scaling both amounts by the same number keeps the ratio true.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t042",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:28:58.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:29:38.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "42",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 43,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's a nice pattern to notice.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t043",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:29:46.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:30:28.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "43",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 44,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So really any scale factor works, not just the one we used for 12 cups.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t044",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:30:30.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:31:04.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "44",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 45,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, so what's the general rule you'd state?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t045",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:31:10.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:32:09.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "45",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 46,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "If flour is some multiple of 3, sugar is that same multiple of 5.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t046",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:32:13.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:32:53.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "46",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 47,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's exactly the relationship behind the ratio.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t047",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:33:01.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:33:53.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "47",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 48,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So for future problems like this, I should first find the scale factor from whichever amount is given.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t048",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:34:01.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:34:35.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "48",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 49,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good, what's the next step after finding the factor?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t049",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:34:37.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:34:55.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "49",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 50,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Multiply the other ratio number by that same factor.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t050",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:35:01.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:35:48.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "50",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 51,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "And how would you find the factor in general?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t051",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:35:54.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:36:36.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "51",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 52,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Divide the given amount by its own ratio number.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t052",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:36:41.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:37:35.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "52",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 53,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "What if the given amount belongs to the other quantity instead?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t053",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:37:38.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:38:20.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "53",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 54,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Then I'd divide by that ratio number instead and multiply the other one.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t054",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:38:23.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:39:15.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "54",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s04",
      "sequence_id": 55,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's a solid general approach to carry forward.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s04-t055",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:39:20.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:40:13.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "55",
